        "# 🧠 Introduction to Natural Language Processing\n",
        "## High School NLP Competition Notebook\n",
        "\n",
        "**Based on:** *Introduction to Natural Language Processing* lecture  \n",
        "**Dataset:** [IMDB Dataset of 50K Movie Reviews](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/lakshmi25npathi/imdb-dataset-of-50k-movie-reviews)\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 📥 How to get the dataset\n",
        "1. Visit the Kaggle link above and download `IMDB Dataset.csv`\n",
        "2. Place the file in the **same folder** as this notebook\n",
        "3. Run all cells from top to bottom\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🏆 Competition Rules\n",
        "- Cells marked with `# TODO` require **your implementation**\n",
        "- Do **not** change cells that are already filled in — they are scaffolding\n",
        "- Each section ends with a **score rubric** so you know what judges look for\n",
        "- Run `Kernel → Restart & Run All` before submitting to make sure everything works\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🗺️ The NLP Pipeline (memorise this!)\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "Raw Text → Tokenise → Pre-process → Feature Extraction → Model → Output/Prediction\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "### The Four Types of Language Ambiguity\n",
        "\n",
        "| Type | Example | Ambiguity |\n",
        "|------|---------|-----------|\n",
        "| **Lexical** | \"I went to the bank\" | Riverbank or financial bank? |\n",
        "| **Syntactic** | \"I saw the man with the telescope\" | Who has the telescope? |\n",
        "| **Semantic** | \"Every student loves a teacher\" | One specific teacher or any? |\n",
        "| **Pragmatic** | \"Can you close the window?\" | Literal question or polite request? |\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cf8803fc"
      }
