        "---\n",
        "## Section 1 — Text Pre-processing Pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Pre-processing** transforms raw, noisy text into a clean, consistent form that a machine learning model can work with.\n",
        "\n",
        "Raw text is full of problems: inconsistent capitalisation (`QuICK`, `QUICK`), repeated punctuation (`!!!`), meaningless filler words (`the`, `a`, `is`), and word variations (`running`, `ran`, `runs`).\n",
        "\n",
        "We fix all of these — in order — before building any model.\n",
        "\n",
        "**The pipeline:**  \n",
        "`Raw text → Tokenise → Lowercase → Remove punctuation → Expand contractions → Remove stop words → Lemmatise`\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2b5d36f6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "20cefd1f",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1 — Tokenisation\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Token**: the smallest meaningful unit of text. Usually a word, but can also be punctuation or a sub-word.\n",
        "\n",
        "`\"I love NLP!\"  →  [\"I\", \"love\", \"NLP\", \"!\"]`\n",
        "\n",
        "Tokenisation is **always** the first step. We use NLTK's `word_tokenize()`.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "20cefd1f"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "406d4d15",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# ── Step 1: Tokenisation — already implemented for you ───────────────────────\n",
        "sample_review = df['review'].iloc[0]\n",
        "print(\"ORIGINAL (first 300 chars):\")\n",
        "print(sample_review[:300])\n",
        "\n",
        "tokens = word_tokenize(sample_review)\n",
        "print(f\"\\nTOKENS (first 20): {tokens[:20]}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Total tokens in this review: {len(tokens)}\")\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
