      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3 — Stop Word Removal\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Stop words** are extremely common words that carry little semantic meaning on their own: `the`, `a`, `is`, `in`, `of`, `and`, ...\n",
        "\n",
        "Removing them reduces noise and speeds up computation.\n",
        "\n",
        "⚠️ **When NOT to remove stop words:**\n",
        "- Sentiment analysis: `\"not good\"` → removing `\"not\"` flips the meaning!\n",
        "- Machine translation: every word matters for grammar\n",
        "- Question answering: `\"who\"` and `\"is\"` are critical\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0c3240b2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "6b4540fc",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# ── Step 3: Stop Word Removal — already implemented ──────────────────────────\n",
        "STOP_WORDS = set(stopwords.words('english'))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Total English stop words in NLTK: {len(STOP_WORDS)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"\\nSample stop words: {sorted(list(STOP_WORDS))[:20]}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "def remove_stopwords(tokens):\n",
        "    return [t for t in tokens if t not in STOP_WORDS and len(t) > 1]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Demo\n",
        "example_tokens = word_tokenize(\"The cat sat on the mat in the corner of the room\")\n",
        "filtered = remove_stopwords([t.lower() for t in example_tokens])\n",
        "print(f\"\\nOriginal tokens : {example_tokens}\")\n",
        "print(f\"After filtering : {filtered}\")\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true,
