      "source": [
        "### Step 4 — Stemming vs Lemmatisation\n",
        "\n",
        "Both reduce words to a base form, but in different ways:\n",
        "\n",
        "| | **Stemming** | **Lemmatisation** |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Method | Chops word endings using rules | Uses a dictionary to find the real base form |\n",
        "| Speed | Fast ⚡ | Slower 🐢 |\n",
        "| Output | May not be a real word (`studi`) | Always a real English word (`study`) |\n",
        "| Use when | Speed matters | Correctness matters |\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{PorterStemmer: } \\textit{studies} \\rightarrow \\textit{studi}$$\n",
        "$$\\text{Lemmatiser: } \\textit{studies} \\rightarrow \\textit{study}$$\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5edfdd24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "56e3ce56",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# ── Step 4: Stemming vs Lemmatisation — already implemented ──────────────────\n",
        "stemmer    = PorterStemmer()\n",
        "lemmatizer = WordNetLemmatizer()\n",
        "\n",
        "test_words = [\"running\", \"studies\", \"better\", \"flies\", \"was\",\n",
        "              \"happily\", \"connection\", \"caring\", \"wolves\", \"leaves\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "rows = []\n",
        "for w in test_words:\n",
        "    rows.append({\"Word\": w,\n",
        "                 \"Stemmed\":      stemmer.stem(w),\n",
        "                 \"Lemmatised\":   lemmatizer.lemmatize(w, pos='v')})\n",
        "\n",
        "comparison_df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "print(comparison_df.to_string(index=False))\n",
        "print(\"\\n→ We will use Lemmatisation for the rest of this notebook.\")\n"
      ],
