        "---\n",
        "## Section 3 — Bag of Words and TF-IDF\n",
        "\n",
        "### What is Bag of Words (BoW)?\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Bag of Words (BoW)**: represent a document by counting how many times each word appears. Word **order is ignored** — only counts matter.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Example:**  \n",
        "`Doc 1: \"the cat sat on the mat\"` → `{the:2, cat:1, sat:1, on:1, mat:1}`\n",
        "\n",
        "BoW works surprisingly well for classification, but ignores the fact that `\"the cat sat\"` and `\"sat cat the\"` are identical in BoW space.\n",
        "\n",
        "### TF-IDF — Smarter Weighting\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{TF}(w, d) = \\frac{\\text{count}(w, d)}{\\text{total words in } d}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{IDF}(w) = \\log\\left(\\frac{N}{\\text{number of docs containing } w}\\right)$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{TF-IDF}(w, d) = \\text{TF} \\times \\text{IDF}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Intuition:**\n",
        "- `\"the\"` appears in nearly every document → very **low** TF-IDF score\n",
        "- `\"photosynthesis\"` is rare but highly informative in biology docs → very **high** score\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "461791b3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "6ccb9ed8",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
