        "---\n",
        "## Section 4 — N-gram Language Model (from scratch)\n",
        "\n",
        "A **language model** assigns a probability to a sequence of words — it quantifies how \"natural\" a sentence sounds.\n",
        "\n",
        "$$P(w_1, w_2, \\ldots, w_n) = P(w_1) \\times P(w_2|w_1) \\times P(w_3|w_2) \\times \\cdots \\times P(w_n|w_{n-1})$$\n",
        "\n",
        "We build three components: **Unigram MLE**, **Bigram MLE**, and **Laplace Smoothing**.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### The Markov Assumption\n",
        "\n",
        "We cannot compute $P(w_n \\mid \\text{all previous words})$ — there are too many combinations.  \n",
        "Instead, we look at only the last $N-1$ words:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Model | Formula | Context window |\n",
        "|-------|---------|---------------|\n",
        "| Unigram | $P(w)$ | no context |\n",
        "| Bigram | $P(w_n \\mid w_{n-1})$ | 1 word back |\n",
        "| Trigram | $P(w_n \\mid w_{n-1}, w_{n-2})$ | 2 words back |\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9b5c0930"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2b81ffb9",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### 4.1 — Unigram Model (MLE)\n",
        "\n",
        "$$P(w) = \\frac{\\text{count}(w)}{N}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where $N$ = total number of tokens in the corpus.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2b81ffb9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4a4a2fca",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# ── Build corpus from training reviews ────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "corpus_tokens = \" \".join(X_train).split()\n",
        "N_tokens = len(corpus_tokens)\n",
        "print(f\"Total tokens in training corpus: {N_tokens:,}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ── Unigram counts & probabilities ────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "unigram_counts = Counter(corpus_tokens)\n",
        "V = len(unigram_counts)\n",
        "\n",
        "def unigram_prob(word):\n",
        "    return unigram_counts.get(word, 0) / N_tokens\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Vocabulary size: {V:,}\")\n",
        "print(\"\\nTop 20 most probable words:\")\n",
        "for word, count in unigram_counts.most_common(20):\n",
        "    print(f\"  P({word:<15}) = {count/N_tokens:.5f}\")\n"
