        "---\n",
        "## Section 5 — Naïve Bayes Classifier\n",
        "\n",
        "### Bayes' Theorem\n",
        "\n",
        "$$P(c \\mid w_1 \\ldots w_n) \\propto P(c) \\times \\prod_{i} P(w_i \\mid c)$$\n",
        "\n",
        "- $P(c)$ = **Prior** — how common is this class in training data?\n",
        "- $P(w_i \\mid c)$ = **Likelihood** — how often does word $w_i$ appear in class $c$?\n",
        "- We predict the class with the **highest score**\n",
        "\n",
        "### The \"Naïve\" Assumption\n",
        "We assume every word is **independent** of every other word, given the class.  \n",
        "This is technically false (words *do* correlate), but it works incredibly well in practice.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Why Log-Probabilities?\n",
        "\n",
        "Multiplying thousands of tiny probabilities causes **floating-point underflow** (the number becomes 0).  \n",
        "Instead, we sum logarithms:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\log P(c \\mid \\text{doc}) = \\log P(c) + \\sum_{i} \\log P(w_i \\mid c)$$\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f5fbbe43"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2dd404d7",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "> 🏆 **TODO 7 (20 points — highest weight!)** — Build a complete Naïve Bayes classifier from scratch.  \n",
        "> No sklearn. Only Python, Counter, and math.log.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2dd404d7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "aa7395b2",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# ── TODO 7: Naïve Bayes from scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "# SCORING: 20 points  ← this is the most important section\n",
        "\n",
        "class NaiveBayesClassifier:\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Multinomial Naïve Bayes for binary text classification.\n",
        "    Uses Laplace smoothing and log-probabilities.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    def fit(self, texts, labels):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Train the classifier.\n",
        "        Args:\n",
        "            texts  : list of pre-processed strings (training set)\n",
        "            labels : list of class labels (same length as texts)\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        self.classes = list(set(labels))\n",
        "        self.log_priors = {}\n",
        "        self.log_likelihoods = {}  # {class: {word: log_prob}}\n",
        "        self.vocab = set()\n",
        "        self.class_token_totals = {}\n",
        "        # TODO Step 1: Count how many documents belong to each class\n",
        "        #              Store in a dict: class_doc_counts = {class: count}\n",
        "        class_doc_counts = Counter(labels)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # TODO Step 2: Compute log prior for each class\n",
        "        #              log P(c) = log(count(c) / total_docs)\n",
        "        total_docs = len(labels)\n",
        "        for c in self.classes:\n",
        "            self.log_priors[c] = math.log(class_doc_counts[c] / total_docs)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # TODO Step 3: For each class, count word frequencies\n",
        "        #              word_counts[c] = Counter of words in all docs of class c\n",
        "        word_counts = {c: Counter() for c in self.classes}\n",
        "        for text, label in zip(texts, labels):\n",
        "            tokens = text.split()\n",
        "            self.vocab.update(tokens)\n",
        "            word_counts[label].update(tokens)  # ← this line is done for you\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.vocab_size = len(self.vocab)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # TODO Step 4: Compute Laplace-smoothed log-likelihoods\n",
        "        #              log P(word | c) = log( (count(word,c)+1) / (total_tokens_in_c + |V|) )\n",
        "        for c in self.classes:\n",
        "            total_tokens_in_class = sum(word_counts[c].values())\n",
        "            self.class_token_totals[c] = total_tokens_in_class\n",
        "            self.log_likelihoods[c] = {}\n",
        "            for word in self.vocab:\n",
        "                self.log_likelihoods[c][word] = math.log(\n",
        "                        (word_counts[c][word] + 1) /\n",
        "                        (total_tokens_in_class + self.vocab_size)\n",
        "                    )\n",
        "\n",
        "        return self\n",
        "\n",
        "    def predict_one(self, text):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Classify a single pre-processed string.\n",
        "        Returns the class with the highest log-score.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        tokens = text.split()\n",
        "        scores = {}\n",
        "        for c in self.classes:\n",
        "            # TODO: start with the log prior\n",
