      "source": [
        "### 6.2 — Pointwise Mutual Information (PMI)\n",
        "\n",
        "Raw co-occurrence counts are biased towards frequent words. PMI corrects for this:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{PMI}(w, c) = \\log_2 \\frac{P(w, c)}{P(w) \\times P(c)}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Positive PMI (PPMI)** = $\\max(\\text{PMI}, 0)$ — we ignore negative values (unreliable in sparse data).\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a8366b6e"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ca1400ac",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# ── PPMI matrix — already implemented ────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "def compute_ppmi(cooc_matrix):\n",
        "    total = cooc_matrix.sum()\n",
        "    if total == 0:\n",
        "        return cooc_matrix\n",
        "    row_sums = cooc_matrix.sum(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n",
        "    col_sums = cooc_matrix.sum(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n",
        "    with np.errstate(divide='ignore', invalid='ignore'):\n",
        "        pmi = np.log2((cooc_matrix * total) /\n",
        "                      (row_sums * col_sums + 1e-9) + 1e-9)\n",
        "    ppmi = np.maximum(pmi, 0)\n",
        "    return ppmi\n",
        "\n",
        "ppmi_matrix = compute_ppmi(cooc_matrix)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 10))\n",
        "sns.heatmap(ppmi_matrix, xticklabels=top30_words, yticklabels=top30_words,\n",
        "            cmap='YlOrRd', ax=ax)\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"PPMI Matrix — Semantic Association Strength\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nTop 5 strongly associated word pairs (PPMI):\")\n",
        "pairs_ppmi = []\n",
        "n = len(top30_words)\n",
        "for i in range(n):\n",
        "    for j in range(i+1, n):\n",
        "        if ppmi_matrix[i, j] > 0:\n",
        "            pairs_ppmi.append((top30_words[i], top30_words[j], ppmi_matrix[i, j]))\n",
        "pairs_ppmi.sort(key=lambda x: x[2], reverse=True)\n",
        "for w1, w2, score in pairs_ppmi[:5]:\n",
        "    print(f\"  ({w1!r:12}, {w2!r:12})  PPMI = {score:.3f}\")\n"
      ],
