        "### 7.2 — Zero-shot Classification\n",
        "\n",
        "With a large enough pre-trained model, you can classify text into **categories the model was never explicitly trained on** — just by describing them in plain English.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "59969e4d"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3097ef2c",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# ── Zero-shot classification ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    zero_shot = hf_pipeline(\"zero-shot-classification\",\n",
        "                             model=\"facebook/bart-large-mnli\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    test_reviews = [\n",
        "        \"The cinematography was breathtaking but the plot made no sense.\",\n",
        "        \"I laughed so hard — this is the funniest film I've seen in years!\",\n",
        "        \"Terrible acting, dreadful script, complete waste of time.\",\n",
        "        \"It was okay I guess. Some parts were good, others not so much.\",\n",
        "        \"I can't believe how bad this was. Oh wait, actually it was great.\",\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "    candidate_labels = [\"positive\", \"negative\", \"mixed\", \"sarcastic\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"Zero-shot classification results:\")\n",
        "    for review in test_reviews:\n",
        "        result = zero_shot(review, candidate_labels)\n",
        "        top_label = result['labels'][0]\n",
        "        top_score = result['scores'][0]\n",
        "        print(f\"  [{top_label.upper():8} {top_score:.2f}] {review[:70]}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "except Exception as e:\n",
        "    print(f\"Zero-shot model unavailable: {e}\")\n"
      ],
